 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Channel selection",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "S3, S2 and S1 form a 3-bit binary code (S1 the lowest bit) that a 1-of-8 decoder turns into one closed switch between Z and Yn, where n is the code. Each switch conducts both ways, so Z may be the input (demultiplexer) or the output (multiplexer)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Enable",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "E is active LOW. While E is LOW the addressed channel is closed; with E HIGH all eight channels are open whatever S1 to S3 hold."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supplies and signal range",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "S1 to S3 and E enter through logic level converters and swing between VSS and VDD; the Y and Z terminals swing between VEE and VDD. The allowed combinations of VDD - VEE and VDD - VSS form a region with corners at (3 V, 3 V), (15 V, 5 V), (15 V, 15 V) and (5 V, 15 V), taken as (VDD - VEE, VDD - VSS)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input clamp diodes",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs have clamp diodes; with a current-limiting resistor in series, an input can be driven from a voltage above the supply."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switch current direction",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "When current enters a Y terminal, hold the switch drop at 0.4 V or below to keep VDD current from flowing out of Z. Current entering Z causes no such effect. Y and Z always stay between VEE and VDD."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ESD protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Human body model (JESD22-A114F): above 2000 V. Machine model (EIA/JESD22-A115-A): above 200 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Standards and ratings",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Static CMOS logic, meets JEDEC JESD 13-B, with parameters given at 5 V, 10 V and 15 V and symmetrical output characteristics. Specified for -40 °C to +85 °C and -40 °C to +125 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Automotive use",
   "page": 17,
   "text": "Not qualified for automotive applications."
  }
 ],
